{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MM4ForceFieldEnergy","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"We always report energy, time, and unit conversion constants in double","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"precision. Potential energy can sometimes have a massive absolute value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that dwarfs the magnitude of relative values. Rigid body bulk properties","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(only accessed by the CPU) are stored in FP64 to minimize drift from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"accumulated rounding error. Everything else is in FP32. Force","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"field parameters are in single precision because we don’t know their values","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with a lot of certainty. In addition, cached parameters may consume a large","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"amount of memory.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Some internal summation algorithms temporarily employ mixed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"precision. Both the CPU code for ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MM4RigidBody"},{"text":" and GPU code for the OpenMM","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Metal plugin use block summation. The majority of the compute cost happens","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on FP32, either to harness more GFLOPS and reduce register pressure","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(CPU) or provide compatibility with a specific hardware vendor (GPU). The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rounding error is capped to whatever error occurs within a block","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(~1000 elements). Outside of the block, the number is casted to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"FP64 and summed with no additional rounding error. This prevents unexpected","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"issues popping up with large systems that exceed 1000 atoms. The mantissa","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of the quantity is still ~24 bits; we just prevent it from degrading to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"~16 bits.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/MM4\/documentation\/MM4"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/mm4\/mm4forcefieldenergy"]}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/MM4\/documentation\/MM4\/MM4ForceFieldEnergy\/kinetic","doc:\/\/MM4\/documentation\/MM4\/MM4ForceFieldEnergy\/potential"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties"}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:3MM40A16ForceFieldEnergyV","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MM4ForceFieldEnergy"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","modules":[{"name":"MM4"}],"title":"MM4ForceFieldEnergy","symbolKind":"struct","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MM4ForceFieldEnergy"}]},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/MM4\/documentation\/MM4\/MM4ForceFieldEnergy","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The energy of a force field."}],"references":{"doc://MM4/documentation/MM4/MM4ForceFieldEnergy/potential":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/MM4\/documentation\/MM4\/MM4ForceFieldEnergy\/potential","title":"potential","url":"\/documentation\/mm4\/mm4forcefieldenergy\/potential","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"potential"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The system’s total potential energy, in zeptojoules."}]},"doc://MM4/documentation/MM4":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MM4\/documentation\/MM4","abstract":[{"text":"Molecular Mechanics force field, version 4. The simulator used to create ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Nanosystems (1992)","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", but updated with modern ab initio parameters.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MM4","role":"collection","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/mm4"},"doc://MM4/documentation/MM4/MM4ForceFieldEnergy/kinetic":{"url":"\/documentation\/mm4\/mm4forcefieldenergy\/kinetic","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"kinetic","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/MM4\/documentation\/MM4\/MM4ForceFieldEnergy\/kinetic","kind":"symbol","title":"kinetic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The system’s total kinetic energy, in zeptojoules."}]},"doc://MM4/documentation/MM4/MM4ForceFieldEnergy":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MM4ForceFieldEnergy","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MM4ForceFieldEnergy","url":"\/documentation\/mm4\/mm4forcefieldenergy","identifier":"doc:\/\/MM4\/documentation\/MM4\/MM4ForceFieldEnergy","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MM4ForceFieldEnergy","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The energy of a force field."}],"kind":"symbol"}}}